Upload a local bundle to a pool on a Bundle Server.

The bundle is verified first, and the server verifies every file before it
publishes the bundle, so a failed push never leaves a partial bundle on the server.

A push that is interrupted can be run again. A server that honours Idempotency-Key
continues the upload and receives only the files it still misses. Any other server
receives every file again in a new upload, and the old one stays open until it
expires.

If the server already holds the bundle nothing is uploaded: its title and tags on
the server stay as they are, and the push succeeds with status "exists".

Version 1 bundles must be migrated first. Bundles without files cannot be pushed.

Examples:
  # Push to the remote named by default_remote
  bundle push /path/to/bundle

  # Push to a specific pool on a specific remote
  bundle push /path/to/bundle --remote origin --remote-pool archive

Configuration:
  Remotes are configured in ~/.config/bundle/config.yaml. The url includes the
  API root. BUNDLE_TOKEN in the environment overrides the token.

  default_remote: origin
  remotes:
    origin:
      url: https://bundles.example.org/api/v1
      token: secret
      pool: default
